urn:agi-folder:disease,disease,Disease,BioPortal: BPT,include,,,clinical_terminology,native,entity_as_process,"bpt:Disease as a subclass of bpt:Pathway focusses on molecular interactions rather than clinical presentation. All bpt:Pathway leafs are proper process-like pathways. But, the classes in between are typically perceived as continuants. Full example: bpt:CCR5 Signaling in Macrophages is_a bpt:blood is_a bpt:Tissues is_a bpt: Anatomy index is_an Index is_a Pathways.",absent,absent,good,good,1,,MM,2026-07-05,,,,,"although denoted as taxonomy, the hierarchy contains false or at least strange is_a relationships.  1. bpt:Wilson's Disease is_a bpt:Wilson's disease.   2. bpt:Oxidative Stress in vitiligo is_a bpt:Vitiligo"
