http://www.semanticweb.org/ontologies/epo.owl#HealthCondition,health condition,health condition,BioPortal: EPO,include,,,curated_ontology,native,entity_as_state,"Terrible wording and largely unintelligible conceptual-graph definition. The class does not read as a disease entity itself, but as a clinical/phenotypic manifestation or diagnostic interpretation of an underlying internal state. However, internal state is modeled as a sibling rather than a superclass or defining substrate, and both health condition and internal state are placed under maternal state. This makes the modelling highly scope-bound to early pregnancy/maternal context, with no clear built-in reusability as a general disease or health-condition class.",partial,absent,partial,good,1,,MM,2026-07-06,,,,,Manual replacement target for EPO syndrome; review HealthCondition instead of Syndrome.
